# NestJS Backend Standards

Follow official NestJS modular architecture. One domain per module (`users`, `students`, `activities`).

- Files: `kebab-case` (`activity-item.entity.ts`)
- Classes: `PascalCase`. Methods/properties: `camelCase`
- DB tables/columns: `snake_case`. Entity properties stay camelCase via `@Column({ name })`
- Never return TypeORM entities from controllers. Map to response DTOs
- Validate with `class-validator` / `class-transformer` on DTOs only, not entities
- Global prefix is `api/v1`. Do not remove it
- Passwords: hash on write, `select: false`, never in responses or Swagger output
- Secrets come from env (`JWT_SECRET`, DB credentials). Never hardcode
- Prefer existing modules/entities. Do not duplicate domain models
- Use CodeGraph MCP (`codegraph_*` tools / CLI) before broad file searches. After schema or module changes, run `codegraph sync`

```typescript
// BAD
@Post() create(@Body() student: Student) { return this.repo.save(student); }

// GOOD
@Post() create(@Body() dto: CreateStudentDto): Promise<StudentResponseDto> {
  return this.studentsService.create(dto);
}
```
